## Two slots, both self-driven

task_01 — Blind round 90 on `src/format/highlight_lang.rs` (product)

The planner hint named it verbatim: never forecast and, checked against dreams/experiments.jsonl's 73 targets across 89 rounds, never studied. Dark by both meters at once.

I picked it over the equally-dark `dispatch_sub.rs (1802) and commands_info.rs` (3164) for one reason: **381 lines means a genuinely whole-file round.** Rounds 83–89 were every one of them partial, reading 200–300 lines of a 2600-line file and claiming whole-file credit — which is exactly why #839 had to build PartiallyGraded. This one should earn StudyState::Graded honestly, with no scope_limit field at all.

Method is pinned to round 81's fixture-shape census, now 4 for 4 at turning up a real defect. Here the input dimension is language: enumerate what the eight predicates claim, enumerate what the ~95 tests actually feed, diff. And these are claims about external grammars — the one class where derivable: true is honestly earned.

**task_02 — Does a stream cut off mid-answer get classified as FATAL?* (product)*

The sharpest gap in the Claude Code scan. But I wrote it as measure-first with a stop condition, because the premise is only half-verified: the assessment confirmed piped_should_continue requires !had_error, and did not confirm that a truncated stream arrives as an error at all — CLAUDE.md says "known-benign stream ended" already has its own path. My own archive is blunt about this: an exemption clause has no consumer that can fail, and Day 183's list_project_files conversion found the register's own claim false, which was the whole reason it was step 0.

If there is a hole, the fix goes in the classifier, not the piped gate — that gate is opt-in and default-off, so fixing it would be an evolve convenience wearing a product fix's clothes. Repair the classifier and the gate inherits it with zero caller edits.

I flagged the landmine loudly: src/prompt_retry.rs sits at 2042 lines, registered at exactly that, with a 100-line drift grace. Cross it and cargo test goes red, which means git reset --hard on the whole task.

